course: dictionary
lesson: 14967
title: Remaking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word remaking means making something again. «Sam's bridge wobbled, so he began remaking it.» Sam is not starting a new model from scratch. He is building the same bridge again, but better.
explain: You can also remake a bed or a cake. «Mum asked me to remake my bed before school.» Pulling off the sheets and making the bed again is remaking it.
explain: A remake is a new version of an old film, song or game. «The studio is remaking the old cartoon with new characters.» The story is familiar, but new people are making it again.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Ask yourself: is something being made again? If yes, remaking fits. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Remaking means making something again.
fact: Remaking can also mean making something in a new or better way.
fact: A remake is a new version of an old film, song or game.
fact: Remaking a shape with the same tangram pieces shows that the area stays the same.
fact: Remake, remakes, remade and remaking all come from the same verb.
exercise: «Sam's model bridge wobbled, so he is remaking it.» What is Sam doing? | Throwing the bridge away for good | Painting the river under it | Counting the bricks in the bridge | *Making the bridge again, to make it better
exercise: A studio is remaking an old film with new actors. What is a remake? | *A new version of an old film | A camera used on set | A film that was never made | A short story for babies
exercise: «Mum asked me to remake my bed.» What does remake mean here? | Make it again | Sell it to a shop | Sleep in it all day | *Make it again, neatly
test: «The cook was remaking the cake that had sunk in the middle.» What does remaking mean? | Throwing the cake in the bin for good | Eating the whole cake | Hiding the cake in a cupboard | *Making the cake again
test: Which phrase means making a new version of an old film? | reading a book | *remaking a film | making a sandwich | washing a car
exam: «The class kept remaking the paper rocket until it flew straight.» Why do they keep remaking it? | Because it is finished | To eat it at lunch | *To improve it until it works | To make it heavier
